This repository is attached to the versioned `lehard/dev-platform` project factory.

## Developer workflow

The repository uses `workflow_profile={{ workflow_profile }}`, `harness_mode={{ harness_mode }}` and `publish_mode={{ publish_mode }}`. Shared lifecycle scripts are versioned in this repository and updated through reviewed Copier releases.

For normal agent work:

```bash
python3 scripts/agent_doctor.py
python3 scripts/start_task.py my-task --task "OpenSpec add-x: 1-3" --scope "backend/..."
python3 scripts/select_checks.py --execute
python3 scripts/finish_task.py
```

`finish_task.py` enforces OpenSpec lifecycle hygiene, re-fetches `origin/{{ main_branch }}` and either creates a PR or performs a guarded direct push according to `.dev-platform.toml`. It never force-pushes or auto-resolves divergence. A completed task list left active blocks publication instead of relying on a reminder.

Platform-managed CI is self-contained in this repository and updates only through reviewed Copier releases; it does not execute `dev-platform@main` or require private cross-repository workflow access.

## Local and cloud verification

Required selected and full checks run locally before publication. Cloud CI is the clean-environment final gate for `publish_mode=pr`; for `publish_mode=direct`, the automatic `main` run is deliberately lightweight and validates platform/OpenSpec health without repeating the full project check set. Direct-mode repositories also keep the stable pull-request `platform-ci` compatibility gate so reviewed maintenance/rollout PRs can satisfy existing required-status protection. Superseded validation runs are cancelled. Use manual workflow dispatch only when an explicit full cloud run is useful. Do not use the narrower cloud workflow or the compatibility PR gate as a reason to skip required local checks or duplicate expensive project full suites without a reviewed repository-specific need.

See `AGENTS.md` and `docs/engineering/`.
